# 🛡️ Interview Integrity Platform — Master Implementation Plan

> **Project:** Coadex 2.0 — AI-Cheating Detection for Live Remote Interviews  
> **Goal:** 5-signal monitoring (Network · Browser · System · Webcam · Typing) with 70–75% lower compute/storage overhead  
> **Stack:** WireGuard · PyShark · MediaPipe Lite · psutil · Chrome MV3 · SQLite · Python 3.11+

---

## 📦 HOW TO USE THIS PLAN

This is chunked into **6 independent build chunks**. Each chunk = one conversation with me. You do each chunk, hand me what I ask for at the end, then we move to the next.

**You tell me:** "Start Chunk X" → I give you exact code to build → You run it → You give me outputs/keys → Next chunk.

---

## CHUNK 1 — Infrastructure & Tunnel Setup
**Duration:** 1–2 days  
**What gets built:** Server setup, WireGuard VPN tunnel, ephemeral key generation  
**You need to give me:**
- An AWS EC2 instance (Ubuntu 22.04, t3.micro is fine for MVP) — OR say "use local" and we'll do localhost testing
- SSH access to that server (or just your local machine)
- Python 3.11+ installed

### Steps

#### 1.1 Server Provision & Base Install
```
Actions:
- Spin up EC2 Ubuntu 22.04 t3.micro (Free Tier)
- Open ports: 51820/UDP (WireGuard), 8000/TCP (API), 22/TCP (SSH)
- Install: python3.11, pip, wireguard, sqlite3
```

#### 1.2 WireGuard VPN Tunnel (Ephemeral Keys)
```
Build: session_tunnel.py
- generate_session_keys(session_id) → creates unique peer keypair
- start_tunnel(session_id) → spins up WireGuard interface
- stop_tunnel(session_id) → tears down interface, revokes keys
- Keys are time-limited (auto-expire at session end)
```

#### 1.3 Session Lifecycle Manager
```
Build: session_manager.py
- create_session(candidate_id) → returns session_id + WireGuard config
- end_session(session_id) → flush logs, revoke keys, clean up
- GET /session/start → returns WireGuard config for candidate
- POST /session/end → triggers teardown
```

#### 1.4 Base FastAPI Backend
```
Build: main.py (FastAPI)
Endpoints:
  POST /session/start
  POST /session/end/{session_id}
  GET  /report/{session_id}
  POST /events/{session_id}   ← receives monitoring events from client
```

**✅ Chunk 1 Done When:** You can `POST /session/start`, get a WireGuard config back, and `POST /session/end` cleans it up.

---

## CHUNK 2 — Network Monitoring Layer
**Duration:** 1–2 days  
**What gets built:** DNS/SNI capture, EMA-based traffic anomaly detection, domain caching  
**Depends on:** Chunk 1 (server running)

### Steps

#### 2.1 Packet Capture Engine (PyShark)
```
Build: network_monitor.py
- capture_dns_queries(interface) → logs domain + timestamp every 5s sample
- capture_tls_sni(interface) → extracts SNI hostname from TLS ClientHello
- Uses PyShark (wraps TShark) — runs on gateway server
```

#### 2.2 EMA Anomaly Detector
```
Build: traffic_analyzer.py
- TrafficEMA class:
    update(new_value) → metric = 0.2*new + 0.8*prev
    is_anomaly() → True if deviation > 2σ from baseline
- Tracks 3 metrics: packet_count, bytes_per_sec, request_frequency
- Triggers alert event when anomaly detected
```

#### 2.3 Domain Cache + Threat Check
```
Build: domain_classifier.py
- LRUCache(maxsize=500) for domain categories
- classify_domain(domain) → "safe" | "suspicious" | "ai_helper"
- Hardcoded AI helper list: chatgpt.com, copilot.microsoft.com, claude.ai, gemini.google.com, etc.
- Optional: VirusTotal free API for unknown domains (1st hit only, then cached)
```

#### 2.4 Compact Event Logger (Binary Format)
```
Build: event_logger.py
- 8 bytes per event: [event_code(1B), ts_delta_ms(3B), value1(2B), value2(2B)]
- EVENT_CODES dict (paste=0x02, tab_switch=0x03, gaze_drift=0x04, etc.)
- CircularBuffer(maxsize=1000) per module
- flush_to_sqlite(session_id) → writes buffer to DB at session end
```

**✅ Chunk 2 Done When:** DNS + SNI are being logged every 5s, EMA anomalies are firing, domain cache hits working.

**🔑 What to give me next:** VirusTotal API key (free tier, optional) OR say "skip threat API"

---

## CHUNK 3 — Chrome Extension (Browser Layer)
**Duration:** 2–3 days  
**What gets built:** Chrome MV3 extension for tab/URL/clipboard monitoring  
**Depends on:** Chunk 1 (backend API endpoint for events)

### Steps

#### 3.1 Extension Scaffold (MV3)
```
Files to build:
- manifest.json (MV3, permissions: tabs, clipboardRead, activeTab, scripting)
- background.js (service worker)
- content.js (injected into pages)
- popup.html / popup.js (optional UI)
```

#### 3.2 Tab Switch Aggregation (NOT logging every event)
```
Build in background.js:
- Track tab_switches_per_minute (rolling window)
- Track avg_focus_duration_sec
- Track suspicious_domains_visited[]
- ONLY send event to backend when: switches > 5 per 10s window
- Store metrics object, NOT individual tab events
```

#### 3.3 Clipboard Paste Detection
```
Build in content.js:
- Listen to 'paste' event
- Flag if: charCount > 200 AND duration < 1s (physically impossible to type)
- Flag if: 3+ pastes in < 30s
- Flag if: repeated identical content
- POST flagged events to /events/{session_id}
```

#### 3.4 Navigation Flow (Delta Encoding)
```
Build in background.js:
- domains_visited[] → indexed list
- transitions[] → [{from_idx, to_idx, duration_sec}]
- Store domain index references, NOT full URLs
- Saves 70% vs storing raw URLs
```

#### 3.5 Focus Change Threshold Alerting
```
- Count focus changes in 10-second windows
- Log ONLY when rate > 5 changes/10s (abnormal)
- Normal focus changes = ignored (99% of data discarded)
```

**✅ Chunk 3 Done When:** Extension installed in Chrome, tab switches aggregate correctly, paste events POST to backend.

**🔑 What to give me next:** The Chrome extension .zip (for me to review if needed) OR just proceed to Chunk 4

---

## CHUNK 4 — System & Process Monitor (Electron Agent)
**Duration:** 1–2 days  
**What gets built:** Cross-platform desktop agent for process scanning, VM detection  
**Depends on:** Chunk 1 (backend + event endpoint)

### Steps

#### 4.1 Process Scanner (psutil)
```
Build: process_monitor.py
- Startup: baseline_hash = hash(frozenset(get_process_names()))
- Every 30s: compare current_hash vs baseline_hash
- If different: compute delta (only NEW processes)
- Log only new processes — NOT entire process list every 30s

BLACKLIST = {
  "zoom", "anydesk", "teamviewer", "rustdesk",
  "vmware", "virtualbox", "obs", "chatgpt", "copilot-app"
}

Storage target: 15MB → 0.5MB per session (99% reduction)
```

#### 4.2 VM Fingerprint (One-Time at Start)
```
Build: vm_detector.py
- check_cpu_flags() → detect hypervisor CPU flag
- check_audio_devices() → look for virtual audio (e.g., "VB-Audio")
- check_disk_model() → look for "VBOX", "VMWARE", "QEMU" strings
- Run ONCE at session start → cache result → never re-run
- Flag in session metadata if VM detected
```

#### 4.3 Electron Wrapper (Optional for MVP)
```
If building desktop app:
- Electron + Node.js shell
- Kiosk mode (disables Alt+Tab, other windows)
- Calls Python agent via child_process
- Shows only interview UI

For MVP: Can skip Electron and run Python agent separately
```

**✅ Chunk 4 Done When:** Process scanner running, VM check fires once at start, blacklisted processes trigger events to backend.

**🔑 What to give me next:** Nothing required — proceed directly to Chunk 5

---

## CHUNK 5 — Webcam Pipeline (MediaPipe Lite)
**Duration:** 2–3 days  
**What gets built:** Face detection, head pose estimation, gaze zone classification  
**Depends on:** Chunk 1 (event logger)

### Steps

#### 5.1 Adaptive Frame Sampling
```
Build: webcam_monitor.py
- Default: 1 FPS (massive reduction from 30fps)
- If anomaly_detected: switch to 5 FPS for 30s burst
- Returns to 1 FPS after burst window

Effect: 97% fewer frames processed
```

#### 5.2 MediaPipe FaceMesh Lite Integration
```
- Use mediapipe.solutions.face_mesh (lite model, not full)
- Detect 468 face landmarks at 1 FPS
- Extract: nose tip, eye corners, mouth corners for pose estimation
- 70% fewer computation tokens vs full model
```

#### 5.3 Head Pose → Gaze Zone Classifier
```
Build: gaze_classifier.py
- Solve PnP (3D→2D projection) using generic face model
- Output: yaw (left-right), pitch (up-down)
- Map to zones: ["center", "edge", "off_screen", "down"]
- Store ZONE only — NOT pixel coordinates

Baseline: avg_pose(first_20_frames) → freeze baseline
Alert only: deviation > 1.5σ from baseline
```

#### 5.4 Attention Window Aggregation
```
Per 5-minute window, output:
{
  "attention_score": 0-100,
  "drift_count": int,
  "off_screen_sec": int,
  "side_glances": int
}
Store aggregate, NOT individual frame events
90% data reduction vs per-frame logging
```

**✅ Chunk 5 Done When:** Webcam running at 1fps, face zones classified, gaze drift events firing on > 1.5σ deviation.

**🔑 What to give me next:** Nothing required — proceed directly to Chunk 6

---

## CHUNK 6 — Anomaly Engine + Dashboard
**Duration:** 2–3 days  
**What gets built:** Scoring engine, correlation rules, report generator, reviewer dashboard  
**Depends on:** Chunks 1–5 all working

### Steps

#### 6.1 Lookup Table Scoring Engine
```
Build: anomaly_engine.py

RISK_TABLE = {
  "paste_small": 2,    "paste_large": 8,    "paste_code": 12,
  "tab_switch_low": 0, "tab_switch_high": 5,
  "gaze_normal": 0,    "gaze_repeated": 6,  "gaze_sustained": 10,
  "domain_safe": 0,    "domain_suspicious": 8, "domain_ai_helper": 15,
  "blacklist_process": 20, "vm_detected": 10,
  "typing_spike": 8,   "idle_anomaly": 3,
}

score = sum(RISK_TABLE[event] for event in buffer)
# Threshold: score > 15 → flag; score > 30 → high priority
```

#### 6.2 30-Second Buffered Windows
```
- Collect all signals per 30s window
- Process buffer together (not real-time)
- Reduces context switches + redundant checks
- 70% reduction in processing overhead
```

#### 6.3 Correlation Bonus Rules
```
# Only checked when base score > 5
if paste_event AND tab_to_ai_domain: score += 5
if gaze_off AND clipboard_paste:     score += 4
if blacklist_process AND typing_spike: score += 6

# Saves 85% correlation analysis (only runs when threshold met)
```

#### 6.4 Baseline Freeze (5-Minute Capture)
```
baseline = capture_first_5min()  # WPM, tab_rate, focus, network
# FROZEN after 5 minutes — never updated
# All anomaly comparisons reference this frozen profile
```

#### 6.5 Report Generator
```
Build: report_generator.py
- Generate human-readable timeline from event log
- Output format:
  | 10:05:12 | Browser | tab_switch | → chatgpt.com | score: 15 |
  | 10:05:40 | Input   | paste      | 350 chars     | score: 8  |
  | 10:06:05 | Webcam  | gaze_drift | 5s off-screen | score: 10 |
- Generate on-demand only (not live)
- < 5 minutes post-session
```

#### 6.6 Reviewer Dashboard (Simple Web UI)
```
Build: dashboard/ (HTML + Vanilla JS or Next.js)
- Session list with risk score badges
- Timeline view of flagged events
- Filter by: High Risk / Medium / Clean
- One-click report export (PDF or JSON)
- Auth: simple JWT login for reviewer
```

**✅ Chunk 6 Done When:** End-to-end works — start session → monitor → end session → report generated with scores and timeline.

